Test 3rd-push? No — this is "first run fills slot A, second fills B" failing at afterSecond. `afterFirst = { a: first, b: null, changed: true }` — nextCompareSlots(afterFirst, second): valid; second.run(2) !== first.run(1); slots.a exists → return { a: slots.b, b: newRun } = { a: null, b: second, changed: true }. Bug in my logic: when B is empty, second run should fill B, not shift A to null-B!

Branch contract: "Pushing when A is empty fills A then B." So:
```
if (!slots.a) return { a: newRun, b: slots.b ?? null, changed: true };
if (!slots.b) return { a: slots.a, b: newRun, changed: true };
return { a: slots.b, b: newRun, changed: true };
```
Fix model.js.

